    "text": "WorldDirector's persistent dynamic object memory allows object state (position, velocity, orientation) to persist across time steps without requiring visual observation at every frame.",
    "topic": "memory persistence"
  },
  {
    "text": "The memory reduces reliance on continuous visual observations by enabling inference of object state during occlusions or skipped frames, but does not necessarily eliminate the need for initial or occasional visual inputs.",
    "topic": "state inference dependency"
  },
  {
    "text": "WorldDirector employs this persistent memory to construct controllable world simulators that function with sparse visual data, thereby enabling operation without continuous visual observation.",
    "topic": "simulator capability"
  },
  {
    "text": "The design maintains object state independently of visual observation in the sense that stored attributes are not reset or lost when objects become unobserved, but it does not imply the system can operate indefinitely with zero visual input.",
    "topic": "independence scope"
  }
]
